SIDIS-RC EvGen (https://github.com/duanebyer/sidis, GPL-3.0), commit 8f9881a: structure functions of the neutron.

The built-in structure-function set "prokudin" (WW-SIDIS, Bastami et al., JHEP 06 (2019) 007) holds the proton's
parton distributions, and sidisgen used it for every target: with "setup.target n" only the nucleon mass
changed, and the cross sections on the neutron came out equal to those on the proton.

With this patch the set takes the target. For the neutron every flavor sum of the structure functions uses the
proton distribution of the isospin-rotated flavor (u <-> d, ubar <-> dbar): f1, g1, gT, h1, the Sivers,
Boer-Mulders, worm-gear and pretzelosity functions alike. Charges and fragmentation functions keep the flavor
of the struck quark. The proton is unchanged; for the deuteron sidisgen now says that the proton set is used.

Check, Born cross sections at 11 GeV in 0.2 < x < 0.3, 2 < Q2 < 3 GeV2, 0.4 < z < 0.6, PhT2 < 0.3 GeV2
(arbitrary units): p pi+ 7.21, p pi- 3.88, n pi+ 4.32, n pi- 3.75. (n pi+ + n pi-)/(p pi+ + p pi-) = 0.73, as
F2n/F2p at this x.

Apply in the source directory with: patch -p1 < sidis-neutron-isospin.patch

